From 9f6ee4d90756973bf65b11ad93e2bf3bbf0bcf71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Arrendondo <brandon.arrendondo@bissell.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 15:23:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] AP: Avoid NULL as snprintf %s argument for BSS transition
 management query

ieee802_11_rx_bss_trans_mgmt_query() only allocates hex when the
candidate list is non-empty:

    hex_len = 2 * (end - pos) + 1;
    if (hex_len > 1) {
            hex = os_malloc(hex_len);
            if (hex)
                    wpa_snprintf_hex(hex, hex_len, pos, end - pos);
    }
    wpa_msg(hapd->msg_ctx, MSG_INFO,
            BSS_TM_QUERY MACSTR " reason=%u%s%s",
            MAC2STR(addr), reason, hex ? " neighbor=" : "", hex);

The ternary only selects the " neighbor=" prefix text; the raw hex
pointer, which stays NULL for an empty candidate list (or on the
os_malloc() failure path), is still passed unconditionally as the actual
%s argument. This is undefined behavior per the C standard; glibc
tolerates it and prints "(null)", but this is unspecified elsewhere.

This could be reached from a station's BSS Transition Management Query
Action frame; an empty candidate list is a normal, minimal, valid frame.

Pass an empty string instead of the NULL pointer to avoid this.

Fixes: 930695662 ("Add BSS-TM-QUERY event to indicate reception of BSS TM Query")
Signed-off-by: Brandon Arrendondo <brandon.arrendondo@bissell.com>
(cherry picked from commit 9f6ee4d90756973bf65b11ad93e2bf3bbf0bcf71)
---
 src/ap/wnm_ap.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ap/wnm_ap.c b/src/ap/wnm_ap.c
index 03768c496..817b5c62a 100644
--- a/src/ap/wnm_ap.c
+++ b/src/ap/wnm_ap.c
@@ -476,7 +476,7 @@ static void ieee802_11_rx_bss_trans_mgmt_query(struct hostapd_data *hapd,
 	}
 	wpa_msg(hapd->msg_ctx, MSG_INFO,
 		BSS_TM_QUERY MACSTR " reason=%u%s%s",
-		MAC2STR(addr), reason, hex ? " neighbor=" : "", hex);
+		MAC2STR(addr), reason, hex ? " neighbor=" : "", hex ? hex : "");
 	os_free(hex);
 
 	if (!hostapd_ubus_notify_bss_transition_query(hapd, addr, dialog_token, reason, pos, end - pos))
